# Build inputs and outputs. package-lock.json is NOT here on purpose: the Nix
# build runs `npm ci` against it, so it has to be committed and has to stay in
# step with package.json.
#
# `dist/` being listed here is load-bearing, not tidiness. Tailwind v4 detects
# its own sources by walking the project and skipping whatever git ignores, so
# an unignored dist/ makes each build scan the PREVIOUS build's CSS and JS and
# re-emit every class it finds there. Measured: 24.3 kB of CSS became 37.5 kB,
# and it would have kept ratcheting. With dist/ ignored, two builds in a row
# produce byte-identical hashed filenames.
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
# LosOS Lab's core, generated by `npm run lab:core` (cargo + wasm-bindgen
# from admin-ui/lab/core); the build step writes it, git never carries it.
src/lab/core-pkg/
# The Lab's WebAssembly libvirt client, generated by `npm run lab:virt`
# (admin-ui/lab/virt-rpc); imported only when a guest starts on that path.
src/lab/virt-pkg/
